	(text "VOLTAGE DIVIDERS (R_TOT ≈ 100 kΩ)\nFORMULA:\n  R2 = R_TOT × V_REF / 5 V\n  R1 = R_TOT − R2\n  (R1 to +5V, R2 to GND)\n\nRESOLUTION:\n  Brake threshold (V_REF = 1.683 V):\n    R2 = 100 kΩ × 1.683 / 5 = 33.7 kΩ → 34.0 kΩ\n    R1 = 100 kΩ − 33.7 kΩ = 66.3 kΩ → 66.5 kΩ\n\n  Power threshold (V_REF = 2.640 V max):\n    R2 = 100 kΩ × 2.640 / 5 = 52.8 kΩ → 52.3 kΩ\n    R1 = 100 kΩ − 52.8 kΩ = 47.2 kΩ → 47.5 kΩ\n\n  Window (V_LOW = 0.25 V, V_HIGH = 4.75 V):\n    R_WH = 100 kΩ × (5 − 4.75) / 5 = 5 kΩ → 4.99 kΩ\n    R_WM = 100 kΩ − R_WA − R_WB = 90 kΩ → 90.9 kΩ\n    R_WL = 100 kΩ × 0.25 / 5 = 5 kΩ → 4.99 kΩ"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
